  help: they share the byte at 0x0; two registers of one mode share a byte only when one is `read`
        and the other `write`, so that a read means one and a write the other; registers of
        another mode of the device go in an alternate group, `in GROUP` after the offset, and are
        checked only against the registers of their group (ADR 0058, 0061)
